-- title:
--   Index of ±Γ₁(M) and elliptic double-coset counts
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number, nonzero, with $5 \le M$. Inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consider the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$ and the subgroup $\langle -1\rangle =$ `Subgroup.zpowers (-1)` generated by the central element $-1$; write $n$ for the index of their join $\Gamma_1(M) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ (the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ and $-1$, i.e. $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$) in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, as a natural number. The theorem asserts the conjunction of two equalities. First, $n = 3\,\#\bigl(\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle ST\rangle\bigr)$, where the right-hand factor is the cardinality of the set of double cosets of the underlying set of $\Gamma_1(M)$ and the underlying set of the cyclic subgroup generated by $S T$, with $S$ and $T$ the standard generators `ModularGroup.S` and `ModularGroup.T` of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Second, $n = 2\,\#\bigl(\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle S\rangle\bigr)$, the double cosets now being taken with respect to the cyclic subgroup generated by $S$. Both cardinalities are `Nat.card` of the corresponding double-coset quotients.
--
--   This is the standard count of the elliptic points of order $3$ and order $2$ on the modular curve $X_1(M)$: for $M \ge 5$ the groups $\langle ST\rangle$ of order $6$ and $\langle S\rangle$ of order $4$ act freely on the cosets $\Gamma_1(M)\backslash\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, so the two double-coset sets have $n/3$ and $n/2$ elements, and they compute the numbers of points of $X_1(M)$ above $j = 0$ and $j = 1728$ in characteristic zero. It is used in the local analysis of valuations on the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\mathbb{C}$, in particular in the determination of ramification indices above the $j$-line.
-- source:
